      "writtenOn": "2017-06-30T15:08:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point.  With Openflow an ID is 64 bits where the low 48 bits are reserved for the switch id and the high 16 bits are up to the implementers.  So we pretty much have 4 hex for the core id.  We could configure each cluster to start with a specific 4 hex number (or having a range of core_ids they can use) to avoid collision.",
      "parentUuid": "5a202591_7b31b70a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 30,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 30,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "4534a4882a843aad827d93bf58510fe4ebcf9bf1",
      "serverId": "2a2bfe1b-c5c2-48ed-9ac8-16438ab24388",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
